# English Suite No. 1 in A major, BWV 806: Bourree I (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a bright, imitative bourree in cut time, two beats to the
# bar, from a quarter upbeat. Slurred pairs of eighths in the theme
# (a8 g# b a), answered in the bass a bar later; long runs of eighths
# over repeated bass notes in the second half. Lively and singing.
#
# Time signature: 2/2, 50 bars in the Mutopia score and in the MIDI,
# counting both endings of the first half. Mutopia places bar 1 before
# the repeat sign and writes the first ending as two bars (16-17: the
# cadence, then bar 1 again with a different bass), the second ending
# as one short bar (18, three beats, plus the quarter upbeat to B).
# Bar 50 is three beats. The MIDI plays the score once, both endings
# in a row, which would sound wrong, so play restores the order.
#
# Repeats: both halves repeated. About 6 KB.
#   play: upbeat to the first ending (0.75-17), the repeat from bar 2
#   (2-15), the second ending and B (18-50.75), B again from its upbeat.
#   Performed bars: A 0.75-18, A repeat 18-32 (score x is x+16),
#   B 32-64.75 (score x is x+14), B repeat 64.75-97 (score x is x+46).
#
# Tempo: half note = 90, about 2:05 with repeats.
# Track times: Richard Egarr (harpsichord, Harmonia Mundi 2013),
# Bourree I on its own track, 2:07, about half = 91 with both repeats
# (confirmed from the Harmonia Mundi track list). Leonhardt (Seon, 1974)
# 3:47 and Andras Schiff (Decca) 4:11 put Bourree I and II on one track,
# so they cannot be split. 90 follows Egarr: eighths 10 frames each.
#
# Structure (my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   1-4     A major, the theme in the top; the bass imitates in 3-4.
#   5-8     to E major, a pause on B in the top (8).
#   9-12    the theme again in the top (= 1-3).
#   13-16   descending sequence; cadence in E major (16, and 18).
#   19-26   B: the theme on E in the top, imitated by the bass, moving
#           through D major to B minor (26).
#   27-31   E major, then A, cadence in A (31-32).
#   32-40   long eighth-note sequences over repeated bass notes: A pedal
#           (32-33), B (36-37), E (39), then D.
#   41-42   cadence in A major.
#   43-46   a closing four-bar phrase; 47-50 repeat it exactly.
#
# Plan: each half full the first time, echoed on the repeat. The
# closing phrase is stated twice in a row in the score (43-46, 47-50),
# so its restatement is an echo every time, as on a second manual.
# Bass imitations brought forward where the bass answers the theme.

pickup 4

tempo 90 2

play 0.75-17 2-15 18-50.75 18.75-50

dyn 1 f            # A first time
lead 3-4 bottom    # the bass imitates the theme
dyn 18 mp          # A repeat (from bar 2), an echo; bar 17 = bar 1
lead 19-20 bottom  # score 3-4: the bass imitation again
broaden 32 0.95    # score 18: the E major cadence before B
dyn 32.75 f        # B first time, from its upbeat
lead 34-35 bottom  # score 20-21: bass imitation
dyn 57 f           # score 43-46: the closing phrase (still full)
dyn 61 mp          # score 47-50: the same phrase, echoed
broaden 64 0.95    # score 50: a breath before the B repeat
dyn 64.75 mp       # B repeat, an echo
dyn 87 f           # score 41-46: full again for the close
dyn 93 mp          # score 47-50: the closing echo, to the end

rit 2 0.8          # the last two bars into the final A
